# Phase 313 (SMART-01..04) — sudoers grant for the smartctl(8) disk-health wrapper.
#
# Grants the desktop/livinityd user (templated from `bruce` to the resolved
# desktop user at install/update time) permission to run ONLY the root-owned
# smartctl wrapper. Drop at /etc/sudoers.d/livos-smart (mode 0440, root:root).
#
# Security model (code-review HIGH-01 fix — matches sudoers.d/livos-desktop-password):
# - The grant is on ONE explicit binary path with NO glob and NO argument wildcard.
#   The wrapper (/usr/local/lib/livos/livos-smartctl.sh, root-owned 0755) validates
#   its device id against DEVICE_ID_RE + a fixed mode enum {read|selftest-short|
#   selftest-long}, then builds the exact smartctl argv itself. No caller-supplied
#   flag can reach smartctl, so the previous `/dev/*` trailing-wildcard hole — where
#   sudoers' `*` (which does not stop at whitespace) let extra flags like `-s off`
#   or `-t vendor,0x40` be appended after the device path — is closed.
# - Because the desktop user cannot rewrite the root-owned wrapper, it cannot hijack
#   the grant. To change a permitted operation, EDIT THE WRAPPER — do NOT broaden
#   this grant back to a raw `smartctl` path or add a glob.
#
# NVMe is read via smartctl auto-detect (the wrapper's `read` mode emits `-a -j`,
# NOT a `-d nvme` passthrough), so no NVMe-specific shape is needed here.
#
# Deploy (fresh): deploy-livinityd.sh installs the wrapper THEN this fragment;
# day-2: update.sh Step 7.10b (content-diff + visudo validate-or-remove). Both
# sed-template the `bruce` subject to the resolved desktop user.
Cmnd_Alias LIVINITYD_SMARTCTL = /usr/local/lib/livos/livos-smartctl.sh

bruce ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: LIVINITYD_SMARTCTL
